# ============================================================
# Agri-Energy Desk — frontend environment
# Copy to  /var/www/agrienergy/repo/deploy/env/ui.env.production
#
# Read twice:
#   • deploy.sh installs it as UI/.env.production before the build, so
#     any NEXT_PUBLIC_* here is inlined into the bundle.
#   • agrienergy-ui.service loads it as EnvironmentFile, so API_URL is
#     also read at RUNTIME by the Node server.
#
# There is no SESSION_SECRET — auth is a Sanctum bearer token held in
# the browser, not a server-side session cookie. There are no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables either: nginx puts the app and the API on one
# origin, so the browser uses the relative "/api/v1".
# ============================================================

# ── Laravel API, at runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the Next server renders public pages FROM, on every request.
# Points at the loopback nginx listener so the call never leaves the
# droplet and skips a TLS round-trip.
#
# If this is wrong or unreachable, pages still return 200 but render
# empty — apiGet falls back rather than throwing. deploy.sh's last smoke
# test checks /projects body size specifically to catch that.
API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1
